{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting","id":1033974,"title":"Sound, Scrying, and Remote Casting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-18T06:08:25-08:00","id":1033974,"title":"Sound, Scrying, and Remote Casting","content":"Questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Does scrying also allow you to hear the subject/sounds in the area? The description only mentions vision, but I don't understand why Space would be biased towards vision only.<br /> <br /> 2) Sensory range allows casting on someone if you can hear them. The reach for Remote range also only mentions 'viewing' the subject. Would casting on a subject you're talking to on the phone with 2 Reach for Sensory + Remote 'Viewing' work, or no?<br /> <br /> Edit: Removed innacurate range limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-18-2017, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T06:33:09-08:00","id":1033980,"title":"","content":"1) I don't know why it shouldn't be allowed to hear either. At my table scrying is full audio video.<br /> <br /> 2) Book doesn't say what actually is a sensory range. What is enough and what is not. Hearing can't pinpoint individuals just as surely as sight (it depends of distances of course).<br /> My take is that the eg speach is not enough to to affect a guy with spells. You could affect the speach itself or maybe even his vocal cords but not <i>him. </i>I see a place for some merits in here though, like a Wits 3, Life 1 - you can now cast sensory spells based purely on hearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:31:52-08:00","id":1033998,"title":"","content":"Yes, Scrying lets you hear the other side. Without Fate 2, it also lets them hear and see you. Scrying can be a conference call!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:32:57-08:00","id":1034000,"title":"","content":"1) I run it as delivering audio as well.<br /> <br /> 2) There isn't a 200 ft limit to sensory range. You can typically cast on a subject based on details you are able to perceive, for instance at a long distance you might be able to transform a man into a mouse but since you can't see his face at that range you wouldn't be able to target his face to give him a big nose. Targeting someone via the phone should work on the same principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:35:15-08:00","id":1034003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting?p=1033998#post1033998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without Fate 2, it also lets them hear and see you.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't. You can choose for it to be two way or one way, Fate makes it selectively two way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:42:17-08:00","id":1034005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting?p=1034003#post1034003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it doesn't. You can choose for it to be two way or one way, Fate makes it selectively two way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sure that Space alone could &quot;select&quot; targets by its own standards too. +1 Reach: Allow everyone that has Strong sympathetic connection to X(person or item of casters choosing) to perceive Scrying window","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:45:52-08:00","id":1034010,"title":"","content":"I allow Scrying to employ all senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:00:58-08:00","id":1034015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting?p=1033980#post1033980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Book doesn't say what actually is a sensory range.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, actually. I'm just not sure if remote 'viewing' is intentionally more limited than sensory range, or if that's an oversight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Advanced Range factor is sensory, meaning that the<br /> mage must be able to directly see, hear, or sense her subject. Viewing<br /> a subject remotely but in real-time, whether by security camera or<br /> magic scrying window, requires an additional Reach </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:08:49-08:00","id":1034020,"title":"","content":"Yea, But when somebody speaks you hear his vocal cords, his hands when he claps and even then you can't really imagine how those hands or face look. IMO it's not so reliable without some kind of enhanced senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:20:47-08:00","id":1034021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting?p=1034003#post1034003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it doesn't. You can choose for it to be two way or one way, Fate makes it selectively two way.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:26:08-08:00","id":1034025,"title":"","content":"I guess it'd depend on the spell. Sound Control to silence that guy trying to have the last clap at a show? Sure. Mind Control to make him leave early? You're going to need better than &quot;the clapping is coming from somewhere around there&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:34:18-08:00","id":1034027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting?p=1034020#post1034020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, But when somebody speaks you hear his vocal cords, his hands when he claps and even then you can't really imagine how those hands or face look. IMO it's not so reliable without some kind of enhanced senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are pretty good at conceptualizing the world in spite of sensory handicaps. Your visual bias is showing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:41:21-08:00","id":1034032,"title":"","content":"Forgiveable as a presumption, though, given that the very name Mages have for forming a spell is Imago.<br /> <br /> Still, yeah, a canny Mage can picture a spell using sound alone or include their own perspective limitations in it. Tricky, maybe worthy of a penalty, but possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:54:50-08:00","id":1034045,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying that you can't do it. Just that not everything can be done like with your body/face example. How do you target a face if you just hear them speak? Seal his mouth, turn sound into fire maybe. The thing is that you can always area cast something. So what that you can't really pinpoint someone by their voice, just nuke him with area spell where you think he is.<br /> <br /> Edit: You can remote cast area spell btw. Sometimes it's to risky and sometimes its everything that you need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-18-2017, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:58:57-08:00","id":1034046,"title":"","content":"One point to make, because we have two ears we can actually have 'sound depth' and can pinpoint the location of the source. Just because we aren't aware of it doesn't mean it doesn't exist. There have been experiments that showcased that humans actually have a limited form of echolication even. <br /> <br /> Plus as mage deals with symbolism hearing someone is just as valid as seeing someone in my opinion. After all in both cases you are detecting something that can be traced back to them. Plus sensory range is not visual range.<br /> <br /> Edit: if you can target someone you can apply the effect of any spell in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:17:32-08:00","id":1034055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting?p=1034046#post1034046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One point to make, because we have two ears we can actually have 'sound depth' and can pinpoint the location of the source. Just because we aren't aware of it doesn't mean it doesn't exist. There have been experiments that showcased that humans actually have a limited form of echolication even.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf you can hear his body moving in a way that lets you visualize it, why not. If you train you can be even good at it, take a merit. But I don't think that its a default state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:31:50-08:00","id":1034070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting?p=1034055#post1034055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIf you can hear his body moving in a way that lets you visualize it, why not. If you train you can be even good at it, take a merit. But I don't think that its a default state.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a more house rule interpretation on your part rather than a raw reading of the materials in my opinion. Sensory range is Sensory range. There is no raw list of things that must be cast with specific Sensory stimulus at Sensory range. It is simply I will apply this spell to a subject in which I can 'sense' with my senses. You are imposing fundemental truths, symbols of truth, upon something and the subject will be affected the same if you see them or not. Or how would an area of effect style spell function if that is not the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:33:05-08:00","id":1034072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting?p=1034070#post1034070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like a more house rule interpretation on your part rather than a raw reading of the materials in my opinion. Sensory range is Sensory range. There is no raw list of things that must be cast with specific Sensory stimulus at Sensory range. It is simply I will apply this spell to a subject in which I can 'sense' with my senses. You are imposing fundemental truths, symbols of truth, upon something and the subject will be affected the same if you see them or not. Or how would an area of effect style spell function if that is not the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does beg the question of why remote viewing works differently though, since as written it requires visual perception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:37:42-08:00","id":1034078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033974-sound-scrying-and-remote-casting?p=1034072#post1034072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does beg the question of why remote viewing works differently though, since as written it requires visual perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree, it may be an error or assumption based on how one imagines scrying to work. ( I didn't realize the spell included sound for instance)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:41:51-08:00","id":1034081,"title":"","content":"It's typically used for seeing stuff, it probably just never even occurred to the author.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T00:08:30-08:00","id":1034479,"title":"","content":"I would not allow remote casting via telephone. Neither by area of effect, nor by direct targeting the person who is speaking. (I would make an exception for doing something to the voice of the person on the telephone).<br /> To form a spell the mage needs to be able to form the imago of the spell. So you need at least some kind of sensory information about either the location or the subject you are talking to. While a blind mage in the street might work perfectly fine with a well trained hearing and echolocation techniques, he just doesn't get enough sensory information out of a phone call. Phones neither use stereo microphones, nor stereo speakers, so any depth information ist just missing. If you have a sophisticated sound recording system at one location and are listening via a good pair of stereo headphones, I might allow it, but just not with a simple phone call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T03:20:03-08:00","id":1034503,"title":"","content":"I'd say you do have sensory information about the subject though, chiefly, whatever he's talking about.<br /> <br /> I think it also briefly establishes a Sympathetic connection so you can work on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T04:21:59-08:00","id":1034519,"title":"","content":"You have exactly one sensory information about the subject: what his or her voice sounds like. Visualizing the subject just from that is a bit difficult, I would say. At least it is not enough for casting via &quot;remote sensing&quot; if we broaden &quot;remote viewing&quot; to other senses.<br /> <br /> Weak sympathetic connections are defined as: &quot;The two subjects have barely touched one another metaphysically; the subjects of a mage\u2019s spells, or items she has used as Yantras. Casual acquaintances, coworkers, replaceable belongings.&quot; A stranger on the phone does not qualify by itself. I do think you can say, that you establish a weak Sympathetic connection for the time you are actually talking to the person. That leaves you with the problem to come up with a Sympathatic Yantra to the subject beforehand, but if you took care of that you are probably good to go.<br /> <br /> I just think that it shouldn't and isn't possible to just call a random person and hit her/him the second he/she answers the phone with a spell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T04:32:30-08:00","id":1034521,"title":"","content":"You're also receiving sensory information on what they're thinking about. <br /> <br /> Having the connection while talking to them is what I meant, yeah. Web Weaver could make the connection last longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T04:39:17-08:00","id":1034522,"title":"","content":"Yeah, or more likely you need Web Weaver to establish at least a weak connection in the first place. I think the physical contact to the soda cup in the example given can be substituted with actively talking to a person on the phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}